  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure will anchor over the region for the weekend,\nresulting in dry weather and near-normal temperatures. Despite\nthe dry weather, there will likely be a high cloud deck so\nsunshine will probably be filtered. Highs over the weekend will\nbe in the 60s, although inland locations along/east of I-71 may\nreach the lower 70s. Overnight lows will be quite chilly in the\nlower 30s to lower 40s. Any near-freezing temperatures will be\nconfined to NE OH/NW PA and increasing clouds will likely\nmitigate any frost where the growing season is still valid.\nOvernight lows will begin to warm Saturday and especially Sunday\nnights with more widespread 40s and lower 50s anticipated.  \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nThe high will drift east by Monday, allowing southerly flow to\nreturn to the local area for early next week. This will allow\ntemperatures to warm further (likely into the 70s). The best \nchance of showers next week will be as a cold front approaches \nand crosses the area Wednesday and Thursday, but warm air \nadvection early in the week will allow potential for a low- end \nrisk of showers Monday and Tuesday. There's still considerable \nuncertainty in the progression of the midweek system and \ntherefore overall confidence in the timing/placement of any \nprecipitation is low at this point.",
